    "created_at": "2019-10-28T23:27:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-10-28T23:27:57Z",
    "body": "In particular, given an element `el` from a now-unloaded document, the test does:\r\n```\r\n    el.setAttribute(\"onclick\", \"(void 0)\");\r\n    log(el.onclick);\r\n```\r\nand the result is null in Chrome and Safari and will soon be null in Firefox, while the spec currently requires it to be a function compiled from the `\"(void 0)\"` string.\r\n\r\nThere's an interesting question as to what should happen if the `setAttribute` call happens _before_ `el`'s document is unloaded and the `onclick` get happens after.",
